Automated real-render evidence: handler-produced Task 5 form/results bytes plus the real built Tailwind/styles, Plotly, shared chart helpers, and production controller were captured as light and dark pages. Required `npx @axe-core/cli` WCAG 2 A/AA, 2.1 A/AA and 2.2 AA audit: 0 violations on both. Live axe: 0 both. Actual copied-data `/whatif` through official start/stop, changed manual disclosure open: 0 scoped axe violations light/dark, one H1 and header/nav/main present, no page errors. Automated results do not override the following manual failures.

FAILURES

F1 — ACCESSIBILITY.md #6 / WCAG 2.2 3.3.2, web/templates/components/whatif/spending_optimizer.html:39-53 and web/static/js/whatif-spending-optimizer.js:57-62. Enabling “Add a temporary monthly amount” makes amount and stop-month inputs required, but neither visible label/help says required. Users discover the new requirement only after submission.

Unified introduced diff:
@@ new web/templates/components/whatif/spending_optimizer.html:39-53
+<label for="spending-boost-amount" ...>Extra each month (today's dollars)</label>
+<input id="spending-boost-amount" ... aria-describedby="spending-boost-help spending-optimizer-status">
+<label for="spending-boost-stop" ...>First month without extra spending</label>
+<input id="spending-boost-stop" ... aria-describedby="spending-boost-help spending-boost-boundary spending-optimizer-status">
+<p id="spending-boost-help" ...>The stop month is the first calendar month without the extra amount. Plan range: ...</p>
@@ new web/static/js/whatif-spending-optimizer.js:57-62
+const enabled = boostEnabled.checked;
+boostAmount.disabled = !enabled;
+boostStop.disabled = !enabled;
+boostAmount.required = enabled;
+boostStop.required = enabled;

