PASS EVIDENCE

- #1: actual full page has one H1, logical H1→H2→H3→H4→H5 hierarchy, and header/nav/main.
- #2-5: scoped headers/native controls; every input/select labeled; missing minimum focused on native invalid submit; server/apply errors use described polite status and relevant focus.
- #8-11, #13: meaning has text; keyboard focus indicators visible; close returns to exact Inspect invoker; chart summaries and tables are adjacent; spending P10/P50/P90/minimum and all eight timeline series match table values; monetary semantics use labels plus dollar formatting.
- #15: zero-duration Plotly transitions and reduced-motion context.
- #16: input invalidation leaves zero result children, aria-busy false, zero aria-pressed graph controls, cleared graph/table, and one matching live message.
- #14/#17: no applicable new banner/modal.
- 375 px: document equals viewport, chart 347.5 px inside 375 px panel, wide tables scroll within their named regions.

OBSERVATIONS

- The responsive page's visual results-before-settings order versus DOM settings-before-results order is byte-identical to master (`web/templates/pages/whatif.html:68-127`); pre-existing, not a Task 5 failure. Task 5's component-local focus order follows its visual order.
- The only scoped aria-hidden text is the decorative `$` prefix; visible/programmatic help still states today's dollars. No hidden-text abuse or screen-reader-only junk found.
- Full evidence: `.superpowers/sdd/2026-09-10-spending-first-optimizer/task-5-a11y-review.md` and `task-5-a11y-artifacts/`.
